WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.264 --> 00:00:03.264
(light piano music)

00:00:05.310 --> 00:00:08.720
- So I was born with a
certain name that only

00:00:09.710 --> 00:00:11.530
my parents use basically,

00:00:11.530 --> 00:00:13.200
that's my legal name.

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:16.420
And then my dad, he's an artist.

00:00:16.420 --> 00:00:19.780
He's always liked naming people,

00:00:19.780 --> 00:00:23.520
he gifts people names,
it's like a blessing.

00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:25.483
And he gifted me a name.

00:00:26.740 --> 00:00:29.038
And then in school I
wanted an American name,

00:00:29.038 --> 00:00:29.871
(upbeat piano music)

00:00:29.871 --> 00:00:31.330
so I went by Alice,

00:00:31.330 --> 00:00:35.823
and that's why I have
essentially three names.

00:00:37.020 --> 00:00:40.550
My name is Nahre Sol,
I'm a pianist composer,

00:00:40.550 --> 00:00:43.650
and I like making videos, writing music,

00:00:43.650 --> 00:00:46.590
and just making stuff

00:00:46.590 --> 00:00:50.843
about music, surrounding music,
anything related to music.

00:00:56.344 --> 00:00:57.864
(light piano music)

00:00:57.864 --> 00:00:59.950
We're gonna go to Manhattan now,

00:00:59.950 --> 00:01:03.113
and this is where I practice pretty often,

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:07.133
it's where I can practice
on acoustic grand piano.

00:01:11.140 --> 00:01:14.911
Okay, my first video was June 2nd, 2017.

00:01:14.911 --> 00:01:15.890
(upbeat piano music)

00:01:15.890 --> 00:01:18.720
And it was a compilation
of what I was practicing

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:20.763
along with shots of my dog,

00:01:22.094 --> 00:01:23.423
and stuff outside.

00:01:25.910 --> 00:01:27.610
I uploaded it because I was bored,

00:01:28.550 --> 00:01:30.053
and I'm a millennial,

00:01:30.053 --> 00:01:31.393
and you do stuff like that.

00:01:34.031 --> 00:01:35.060
I don't know,

00:01:35.060 --> 00:01:37.010
why do people watch (laughs) my videos?

00:01:38.344 --> 00:01:41.427
(upbeat piano music)

00:01:44.010 --> 00:01:46.780
I can't speak for my viewers,

00:01:46.780 --> 00:01:49.410
but maybe part of what's interesting

00:01:49.410 --> 00:01:52.210
is that someone from the
classical music world

00:01:52.210 --> 00:01:54.390
is doing other genres.

00:01:54.390 --> 00:01:56.563
Because as a classical musician,

00:01:58.110 --> 00:02:01.430
generally speaking, of course
there are tons of exceptions,

00:02:01.430 --> 00:02:04.670
but generally speaking,
classical musicians

00:02:04.670 --> 00:02:09.043
are quite insular in terms
of what they listen to,

00:02:09.043 --> 00:02:10.870
what music they expose themselves to,

00:02:10.870 --> 00:02:12.880
what music that they play.

00:02:12.880 --> 00:02:15.533
YouTube has changed my life completely.

00:02:16.457 --> 00:02:19.624
(laughs) I'm kidding.

00:02:29.450 --> 00:02:31.580
Oh, that's a great question,

00:02:31.580 --> 00:02:35.310
would I rather listen
to music or play music?

00:02:35.310 --> 00:02:36.253
I think listen.

00:02:38.500 --> 00:02:41.520
I'm obviously really
attached to the piano, but

00:02:43.080 --> 00:02:45.763
I like music more than I do the piano.

00:02:46.700 --> 00:02:49.333
And I like writing more than I do playing.

00:02:50.570 --> 00:02:53.310
A lot of times when I'm writing I want to,

00:02:53.310 --> 00:02:55.830
there's a certain sound that I wanna hear

00:02:55.830 --> 00:02:58.310
that maybe I'll first try to find

00:02:59.370 --> 00:03:02.840
on Spotify or YouTube, or somewhere else.

00:03:02.840 --> 00:03:05.903
And then other times I just
write stuff that comforts me.

00:03:12.020 --> 00:03:15.280
A lot of stuff that we
go through emotionally

00:03:15.280 --> 00:03:18.030
in our daily lives is very complicated.

00:03:18.030 --> 00:03:21.560
But even when we're feeling happy or

00:03:23.500 --> 00:03:25.883
sad, it's very complicated.

00:03:26.730 --> 00:03:30.250
So to create something that matches that,

00:03:30.250 --> 00:03:32.950
I think music is helpful

00:03:33.840 --> 00:03:35.750
'cause you can create something that is

00:03:37.130 --> 00:03:40.440
light and warm, but with an undertone

00:03:40.440 --> 00:03:43.640
of something unsettling,

00:03:43.640 --> 00:03:48.640
but also hopeful, but kinda
pessimistic, but happy.

00:03:48.850 --> 00:03:50.980
You know, it's complicated.

00:03:50.980 --> 00:03:53.420
So it's just finding a medium

00:03:53.420 --> 00:03:56.043
that compliments how you're feeling.

00:03:57.591 --> 00:04:00.674
(upbeat piano music)

00:04:05.440 --> 00:04:07.580
So when I am here,

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:12.547
I am basically in this room 24/7,

00:04:13.730 --> 00:04:15.850
I just got to the bathroom,

00:04:15.850 --> 00:04:18.520
and I don't spend any time outside,

00:04:18.520 --> 00:04:20.060
I don't use the kitchen at all.

00:04:20.060 --> 00:04:22.494
So when I'm here, I'm here.

00:04:22.494 --> 00:04:23.327
(upbeat piano music)

00:04:23.327 --> 00:04:26.580
This is my keyboard, a CP88,

00:04:26.580 --> 00:04:28.230
I really like it.

00:04:28.230 --> 00:04:30.933
This is my computer
that I do everything on.

00:04:32.530 --> 00:04:33.720
Whoops.

00:04:33.720 --> 00:04:34.620
This is my camera.

00:04:36.570 --> 00:04:40.240
This is my favorite small keyboard.

00:04:40.240 --> 00:04:41.370
Is it on?

00:04:41.370 --> 00:04:43.100
No, it's not plugged in.

00:04:43.100 --> 00:04:44.830
I do a lot of videos on this one,

00:04:44.830 --> 00:04:46.890
and I still really like it.

00:04:46.890 --> 00:04:47.860
It's cute.

00:04:47.860 --> 00:04:49.080
That's the most important thing (laughs)

00:04:49.080 --> 00:04:50.483
about it, it's cute.

00:04:54.710 --> 00:04:55.893
Wanna show the guitar.

00:04:58.180 --> 00:04:59.430
I bought a little guitar.

00:05:00.346 --> 00:05:02.483
It's a kid guitar,

00:05:03.590 --> 00:05:05.510
'cause I wanna learn guitar.

00:05:05.510 --> 00:05:07.847
It's my favorite instrument actually.

00:05:07.847 --> 00:05:10.930
(somber piano music)

00:05:19.049 --> 00:05:21.070
And I remember my first teacher

00:05:21.070 --> 00:05:22.980
didn't really teach me anything.

00:05:22.980 --> 00:05:24.700
The only thing I can remember about her

00:05:24.700 --> 00:05:28.170
was that she had this giant
mole on the back of her neck,

00:05:28.170 --> 00:05:30.290
so when she was teaching me,

00:05:30.290 --> 00:05:31.540
so you'd be standing, right,

00:05:31.540 --> 00:05:32.550
and she's demonstrating.

00:05:32.550 --> 00:05:35.607
I was so bored that I would
just look at her mole (laughs).

00:05:36.750 --> 00:05:41.120
My parents were not typical stage parents.

00:05:41.120 --> 00:05:42.560
Is that what they're called?

00:05:42.560 --> 00:05:43.500
- Uh-huh.
- Yeah.

00:05:43.500 --> 00:05:46.893
I didn't practice that much
until I went to high school.

00:05:47.770 --> 00:05:49.610
So when I first started I would practice

00:05:49.610 --> 00:05:53.090
maybe 45 minutes a day, not even an hour

00:05:53.090 --> 00:05:55.150
for the longest time.

00:05:55.150 --> 00:05:56.900
The simplest I could put it is that

00:05:58.330 --> 00:05:59.670
I'm not the most talented,

00:05:59.670 --> 00:06:03.293
but I make up for it.

00:06:16.670 --> 00:06:19.770
I think what I want to
accomplish is rather simple,

00:06:19.770 --> 00:06:22.830
I just wanna spread enthusiasm

00:06:24.110 --> 00:06:27.410
about music, for music,
the love for music.

00:06:27.410 --> 00:06:28.243
I think

00:06:29.220 --> 00:06:31.270
there's always room for that.

00:06:31.270 --> 00:06:33.040
Where this will all lead,

00:06:33.040 --> 00:06:35.500
I have no idea, I just know that

00:06:35.500 --> 00:06:37.760
I want to keep refining my skills

00:06:37.760 --> 00:06:41.190
and get to a place where I'm writing music

00:06:41.190 --> 00:06:45.140
that I wanna hear, and that I think can

00:06:47.330 --> 00:06:50.510
be a nice addition to the
music that's out there.

00:06:50.510 --> 00:06:53.910
I think it's an obsession, I just like it.

00:06:53.910 --> 00:06:57.203
I feel very comfortable with music.

00:06:58.125 --> 00:07:01.480
I feel happy, I know it's
cliche, but I feel happy.

00:07:01.480 --> 00:07:03.360
Music is kinda like eating,

00:07:03.360 --> 00:07:04.610
but you don't need food,

00:07:04.610 --> 00:07:06.640
you don't necessarily
need food to survive,

00:07:06.640 --> 00:07:08.593
you can be plugged into an IV,

00:07:09.510 --> 00:07:10.720
or what is it called?

00:07:10.720 --> 00:07:12.470
Whatever, the, the little (laughs),

00:07:13.570 --> 00:07:17.400
something that provides nutrition for you.

00:07:17.400 --> 00:07:18.833
So if I didn't have music,

00:07:19.720 --> 00:07:22.250
I think another thing like music

00:07:22.250 --> 00:07:26.957
will provide what music provides
for me to live (laughs).

00:07:27.930 --> 00:07:28.903
Does that make sense?

